<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49736" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uncātus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		uncus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>bent inwards</i>, <i>hooked</i>, <i>curved</i> (post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lanceae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 4, 20</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>bent down</i>, <i>bowed down</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut quidam uncati permaneant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Tard. 5, 3, 57</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>hooked</i>, <i>barbed</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">syllogismi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 9, 9 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
